{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from","id":817732,"title":"Where does Firedust come from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T10:22:56-08:00","id":817732,"title":"Where does Firedust come from?","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if no books ever described where Firedust actually comes from. But if nothing does describe it, where would you have it come from in your game?<br /> <br /> Is it a mineral that is mined out of rocks?<br /> Does it come from rare plants?<br /> Does it only occur near the Wyld?<br /> Is it conjured from nothingness?<br /> <br /> I would probably have it be some combination of these things, but where does it originate for your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:48:05-08:00","id":817760,"title":"","content":"In canon it blows into the south on wind carried from the wyld. In 3rd there are &quot;nodules&quot; of it in the deep south deserts. It can also be replicated via alchemy. Oh and there are snakes that are invisible that eat it and thier poison melts you from the inside out.<br /> <br /> If we didnt know much about firedust i would slap a dune worm scenario on it and see how that plays out. I think i still am doing that in my game it just hasnt come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:58:28-08:00","id":817769,"title":"","content":"Which canon? 2e is no longer canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:04:21-08:00","id":817773,"title":"","content":"Alright, from the Ex3 book... There's mentions that Firedust is more common in the deep South... There's mention of Zoatham and the Galta hills containing a lot of Firedust deposits, which suggest that firedust is dug up rather than it blowing in from the Wyld...<br /> <br /> Then the other mentions of it in relation to its use with firewands (such as how scavenging for it using the dynamic reload actions is pretty much impossible), a mention of it briefly in Righteous Devil Style, and mention in the Panoply chapter that it's Resources 1 in the South, Resources 2 elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:16:24-08:00","id":817780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=817769#post817769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which canon? 2e is no longer canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering he asked which bookS plural in his original post and if were going to get suuuuper pedantic there are technically 0 books published for 3rd edition. I just took the comment at face value and gave him the info i remembered from the last 15 years of the gameline. <br /> <br /> Also its been explicitly said that certain books from 1e and 2e are still canon. To the point of them being kickstarter backer rewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:29:59-08:00","id":817788,"title":"","content":"This is Exalted, so I would say there's a high likelihood that something just shits out firedust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:38:24-08:00","id":817790,"title":"","content":"I always saw Firedust as some kind of special confluence of essence from the Elemental Pole of Fire and particular, naturally occurring mineral deposits. No doubt there's been weird stuff that creates Firedust in other special ways, but that's how I've always thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11006-bowerbird","name":"Bowerbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:38:31-08:00","id":817791,"title":"","content":"In my game, I like to think of the &quot;deposits&quot; as drifts that collect between the dunes. There could be little nodes in the hills if they get covered by sand and compacted over the years.<br /> <br /> Don't mine with open headlamps is what I'm saying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:59:13-08:00","id":817802,"title":"","content":"I would assume its mined but honestly the idea of it being something like sand altered by the elemental pole of fire that drifts into Creation is far more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:19:11-08:00","id":817822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=817760#post817760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we didnt know much about firedust i would slap a dune worm scenario on it and see how that plays out. I think i still am doing that in my game it just hasnt come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would sooo support this idea. Sand-Worm Behemoths in the south would fit ideally in an Exalted game in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:22:35-08:00","id":817827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=817769#post817769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e is no longer canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is until 3rd Edition releases.<br /> <br /> Which it still hasn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:10:54-08:00","id":817888,"title":"","content":"I'm open to ideas from previous editions, even if they change in 3rd ed. Though I suppose the more likely result, based on the path the writers have taken thusfar, is that they will just NOT describe where it comes from and leave it mysterious. Hence, why I asked what you'd choose if it wasn't explicit. Thanks for the responses so far folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:41:10-08:00","id":817911,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure &quot;firedust&quot; is a descriptive rather than proscriptive term -- that is, there's a bunch of different things that behave similarly, all of which get called firedust. Probably they all have different levels of effectiveness, and trade wars get fought over high-grade versus low-grade stuff, but then it all gets abstrated to doing the same damage in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> It seems to blow in from the Wyld and accumulate on Southern dunes; it's dug up in nodules as well (but that may just be in areas that haven't been harvested previously; where centuries of buildup has accumulated). It can be alchemically synthesized and certain animals or plants seem to produce it naturally as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:29:13-08:00","id":818003,"title":"","content":"Well, when a handsome ifrit swipes right on a lonely dust bunny's Tinder profile...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:28:48-08:00","id":818040,"title":"","content":"One form of firedust is bits of skin shed from the Elemental Dragon of Fire. Normally this is a slow process, and it is caught by southern winds and builds in in the dunes of the South. But there is that rare time something agitates the Fire Dragon's scales and it moults its skin all in one go, rubbing against the Pole of Fire to precipitate this event. Finding the Dragon's skin is a bounty of firedust like none other, of the highest grade. Easily the ransom of kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:04:29-08:00","id":818066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=817822#post817822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would sooo support this idea. Sand-Worm Behemoths in the south would fit ideally in an Exalted game in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>(A large explosion occurs)<br /> <br /> &quot;Now that's what I call spice!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:09:11-08:00","id":818071,"title":"","content":"All of these fantastical origins are putting me in mind of what ancient western peoples thought about where cinnamon came from (in a sense that branches from a preference for it to be relatively mundane)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:37:07-08:00","id":818087,"title":"","content":"<i>CoCD: Underworld</i> introduced Firedust Phantoms, which are clouds of plasmic firedust, charged with a suicidal urge to find the nearest animate creature, envelop its newfound victim, and steer it into a source of fire.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine harvesting it is <i>easy</i>, but it almost certainly could be done if you're clever enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:57:57-08:00","id":818098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=817911#post817911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure &quot;firedust&quot; is a descriptive rather than proscriptive term -- that is, there's a bunch of different things that behave similarly, all of which get called firedust. Probably they all have different levels of effectiveness, and trade wars get fought over high-grade versus low-grade stuff, but then it all gets abstrated to doing the same damage in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> It seems to blow in from the Wyld and accumulate on Southern dunes; it's dug up in nodules as well (but that may just be in areas that haven't been harvested previously; where centuries of buildup has accumulated). It can be alchemically synthesized and certain animals or plants seem to produce it naturally as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there are also materials that can be used as firedust <i>or</i> for some other purpose, where using it to load a firewand is technically feasible but is rather the equivalent of grinding up the Koh-i-Noor for industrial abrasive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:12:56-08:00","id":818110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/817732-where-does-firedust-come-from?p=818087#post818087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>CoCD: Underworld</i> introduced Firedust Phantoms, which are clouds of plasmic firedust, charged with a suicidal urge to find the nearest animate creature, envelop its newfound victim, and steer it into a source of fire.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine harvesting it is <i>easy</i>, but it almost certainly could be done if you're clever enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds fucking amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:56:07-08:00","id":818131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=